---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FAQBlock from '../components/FAQBlock.astro';
import RelatedArticles from '../components/RelatedArticles.astro';
import CourseCTA from '../components/CourseCTA.astro';

export const title = "Best Mirrorless Camera Under ₹1 Lakh in India (2026)";
export const category = "camera";
export const description = "Top 3 mirrorless cameras under ₹1,00,000 for filmmaking in 2026 — full comparison of sensor, 4K, Log profile, autofocus aur value for money with buying links.";
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>

<header>
  <h1>Best Mirrorless Camera Under ₹1,00,000 in India — Top 3 Picks for Filmmakers (2026)</h1>
  <p class="hero-subtitle">₹1 lakh ke budget mein sabse balanced mirrorless pick hai <strong>Sony ZV-E10 II</strong> — agar aapko flip-out screen, achhi autofocus aur real 4K10-bit chahiye. Lekin agar stills bhi serious hain toh Canon EOS R50 aur Fujifilm X-S20 bhi strong contenders hain.</p>
</header>

<article class="wrap">

  <div class="callout"><b>Quick take:</b> Solo content creators ke liye Sony ZV-E10 II sabse safe bet hai. Agar hybrid stills+video chahiye toh Fujifilm X-S20 (film simulations + IBIS) best hai. Aur agar Canon ecosystem mein already invest ho chuke ho toh EOS R50 fits perfectly.</div>

  <h2>Quick Comparison Table</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Camera</th><th>Price Range</th><th>Sensor</th><th>Video</th><th>Log/Flat Profile</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>Sony ZV-E10 II</b></td><td>~₹95,000 (body)</td><td>26MP APS-C</td><td>4K/60p (no crop)</td><td class="win">✅ S-Log2/S-Log3</td><td>Vlogging, run-n-gun</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Fujifilm X-S20</b></td><td>~₹1,10,000 (body, often bundled near 1L)</td><td>26MP APS-C X-Trans</td><td>6.2K open-gate</td><td class="win">✅ F-Log2</td><td>Hybrid shooters, colour science lovers</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Canon EOS R50</b></td><td>~₹65,000-75,000 (kit)</td><td>24.2MP APS-C</td><td>4K/30p oversampled</td><td>❌ No true Log</td><td>Canon ecosystem, beginners</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>1. Sony ZV-E10 II — The All-Rounder Vlogging Machine</h2>
  <div class="cam-card">
    <div class="cam-head">
      <div>
        <span class="rank-pill">#1 · BEST OVERALL</span>
        <div class="cam-title">Sony ZV-E10 II (Body/Kit)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cam-price">~₹95,000</div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec-strip">
      <span class="spec-chip">26MP APS-C</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">4K/60p no crop</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">S-Log2/S-Log3</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">10-bit 4:2:2</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Product Showcase AF</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Mic + headphone jack</span>
    </div>
    <p>Yeh camera ZV-E10 ka seedha upgrade hai — sensor 26MP hua, processor BIONZ XR aaya, aur sabse bada difference: ab <b>4K/60p bina crop ke</b> milta hai. Yeh feature khud iss price bracket mein rare hai. E-mount hone ki wajah se Sony ke poore APS-C aur full-frame lens ecosystem tak access milta hai.</p>
    <p><strong>Colorist ka nazariya:</strong> 10-bit 4:2:2 internal recording ka matlab hai grading mein banding ka risk kaafi kam ho jaata hai — heavy secondary grades bhi yeh footage handle kar leta hai. S-Log3 shoot karke <a href="/davinci-resolve-white-balance-method-2026">white balance ko DaVinci Resolve mein sahi lock</a> karna seekh lo toh output professional level tak jaa sakta hai.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>Bina crop 4K/60p — is price range mein unusual</li>
        <li>10-bit 4:2:2 internal — grading-friendly</li>
        <li>Headphone jack + mic input dono</li>
        <li>Reliable subject-tracking autofocus</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div class="pc-box con"><h4>Cons</h4><ul>
        <li>No viewfinder (rear screen only)</li>
        <li>Body plasticky, not weather-sealed</li>
        <li>Battery life average — spare battery zaroori</li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="buy-row">
      <a class="buy-btn" href="https://www.amazon.in/s?k=Sony+ZV-E10+II" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Amazon</a>
      <a class="buy-btn alt" href="https://www.flipkart.com/search?q=Sony%20ZV-E10%20II" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Flipkart</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>2. Fujifilm X-S20 — The Hybrid Colour Science Pick</h2>
  <div class="cam-card">
    <div class="cam-head">
      <div>
        <span class="rank-pill">#2 · BEST COLOUR SCIENCE</span>
        <div class="cam-title">Fujifilm X-S20 (Body)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cam-price">~₹1,05,000-1,15,000</div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec-strip">
      <span class="spec-chip">26MP X-Trans</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">6.2K open-gate</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">F-Log2</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">IBIS</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Film Simulations</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Mic + headphone jack</span>
    </div>
    <p>Fujifilm ka sabse bada selling point unki <b>Film Simulation modes</b> hain — Eterna, Classic Chrome, Nostalgic Neg — jo bina grading ke bhi footage ko ek cinematic look de dete hain. Iske saath in-body stabilisation (IBIS) hai jo handheld gimbal-less shooting ko kaafi smooth bana deta hai.</p>
    <p><strong>Colorist ka nazariya:</strong> F-Log2 wide dynamic range capture karta hai, aur agar aap <a href="/3-what-is-log">Log footage grading</a> ke fundamentals samajhte ho toh yeh sensor bahut room deta hai skin tones ke liye. Open-gate 6.2K recording ka matlab hai reframing flexibility bhi milti hai post mein.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>In-body stabilisation — gimbal ki zaroorat kam</li>
        <li>Film Simulations — quick cinematic look</li>
        <li>6.2K open-gate for reframing</li>
        <li>Vari-angle screen + headphone jack</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div class="pc-box con"><h4>Cons</h4><ul>
        <li>Price aksar 1 lakh se thoda upar chala jaata hai</li>
        <li>Menu system Sony/Canon se different, learning curve hai</li>
        <li>Rolling shutter noticeable hai fast pans mein</li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="buy-row">
      <a class="buy-btn" href="https://www.amazon.in/s?k=Fujifilm+X-S20" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Amazon</a>
      <a class="buy-btn alt" href="https://www.flipkart.com/search?q=Fujifilm%20X-S20" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Flipkart</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Canon EOS R50 — The Budget-Conscious Canon Pick</h2>
  <div class="cam-card">
    <div class="cam-head">
      <div>
        <span class="rank-pill">#3 · BEST VALUE</span>
        <div class="cam-title">Canon EOS R50 (RF-S 18-45mm Kit)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cam-price">~₹65,000-75,000</div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec-strip">
      <span class="spec-chip">24.2MP APS-C</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">4K/30p oversampled</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Dual Pixel AF II</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">No Log</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Compact body</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Mic-in only</span>
    </div>
    <p>Agar budget bachaana hai aur Canon ka reliable autofocus chahiye, toh R50 sabse practical pick hai — yahaan tak ki full 1 lakh bhi kharch nahi hota, kit lens ke saath. Dual Pixel AF II is price range mein best-in-class subject tracking deta hai, jo interview aur run-n-gun content ke liye kaam aata hai.</p>
    <p><strong>Reality check:</strong> Canon Log yahaan available nahi hai, toh grading room limited rahega. Agar heavy color grading priority hai, toh yeh camera Sony ya Fuji jitna flexible nahi hoga — lekin agar priority reliable autofocus aur straightforward "shoot and post" workflow hai, toh yeh sabse kam friction wala option hai.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>Best-in-class autofocus tracking is budget mein</li>
        <li>Halka aur compact — travel-friendly</li>
        <li>Canon ka bada, affordable RF-S lens lineup</li>
        <li>Sabse zyada budget bachaata hai is list mein</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div class="pc-box con"><h4>Cons</h4><ul>
        <li>No Canon Log — grading flexibility kam</li>
        <li>No headphone jack for monitoring</li>
        <li>No IBIS — lens stabilisation pe depend</li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="buy-row">
      <a class="buy-btn" href="https://www.amazon.in/s?k=Canon+EOS+R50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Amazon</a>
      <a class="buy-btn alt" href="https://www.flipkart.com/search?q=Canon%20EOS%20R50" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Flipkart</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Kya Dekhna Chahiye ₹1 Lakh Ke Budget Mein</h2>
  <h3>1. 10-bit vs 8-bit Recording</h3>
  <p>Is budget range mein 10-bit internal recording milna shuru ho jaata hai (jaise ZV-E10 II mein) — yeh heavy grading ke liye game-changer hai kyunki banding aur color-shift risk kaafi kam ho jaata hai.</p>
  <h3>2. Autofocus Reliability</h3>
  <p>Solo shooting ya interviews ke liye eye-tracking autofocus non-negotiable hai. Canon aur Sony dono strong hain yahaan, Fujifilm thoda peeche.</p>
  <h3>3. Ecosystem aur Lens Availability</h3>
  <p>Jis brand ka lens ecosystem local market mein zyada easily milta hai (rent ya buy), usi brand mein invest karna long-term mein sasta padta hai.</p>
  <h3>4. IBIS (In-Body Image Stabilisation)</h3>
  <p>Agar bina gimbal ke handheld shoot karna hai, toh IBIS wali body (Fujifilm X-S20) kaafi farak dalti hai.</p>

  <FAQBlock items={[
    {q: "₹1 lakh mein sabse achhi mirrorless camera kaunsi hai filmmaking ke liye?", a: "Sony ZV-E10 II sabse balanced pick hai — bina crop 4K/60p, 10-bit recording aur S-Log profiles milte hain is budget mein."},
    {q: "Kya Fujifilm X-S20 beginners ke liye sahi hai?", a: "Haan, lekin menu system thoda different hai Sony/Canon se. Colour science aur IBIS ke liye yeh best hai agar learning curve se dikkat nahi."},
    {q: "Canon EOS R50 mein Log profile kyun nahi hai?", a: "Canon apne Log profiles higher-end R-series bodies (R7, R6 II, R5) ke liye reserve karta hai. R50 entry-level positioning follow karta hai."},
    {q: "Kya is budget mein full-frame camera milegi?", a: "Nahi, ₹1 lakh mein full-frame sensor wali reliable video-first camera milna mushkil hai — APS-C hi best value deta hai is range mein."}
  ]} />

  <RelatedArticles links={[
    {href: "/best-mirrorless-camera-under-2-lakh-2026", title: "Best Mirrorless Camera Under ₹2,00,000 (2026)"},
    {href: "/dslr-vs-mirrorless-vs-cinema-camera-2026", title: "DSLR vs Mirrorless vs Cinema Camera — Which to Buy"},
    {href: "/sensor-size-full-frame-vs-aps-c-vs-m43", title: "Full-Frame vs APS-C vs Micro Four Thirds Explained"},
    {href: "/how-to-choose-first-camera-beginner-filmmaker", title: "How to Choose Your First Camera as a Beginner"},
    {href: "/best-camera-for-youtube-vlogging-india-2026", title: "Best Camera for YouTube Vlogging in India"}
  ]} />

  <CourseCTA text="Camera choose ho gayi? Ab uski footage ko professional grade dena seekho DaVinci Resolve mein." />

</article>

</Layout>
